---Settings that control how conversions are counted. All post-click conversions will be counted. A percentage value can be set for post-view conversions counting.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ConversionCountingConfig
---@field floodlightActivityConfigs? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.TrackingFloodlightActivityConfigList The Floodlight activity configs used to track conversions. The number of conversions counted is the sum of all of the conversions counted by all of the Floodlight activity IDs specified in this field. This field can't be updated if a custom bidding algorithm is assigned to the line item. If you set this field and assign a custom bidding algorithm in the same request, the floodlight activities must match the ones used by the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field primaryAttributionModelId? string Optional. The attribution model to use for conversion measurement. This attribution model will determine how conversions are counted. The Primary model can be set by you for a floodlight config or group. More details [here](https://support.google.com/displayvideo/answer/7409983). Only applicable to Demand Gen line items.
---@field postViewCountPercentageMillis? string The percentage of post-view conversions to count, in millis (1/1000 of a percent). Must be between 0 and 100000 inclusive. For example, to track 50% of the post-click conversions, set a value of 50000.

---Counter event of the creative.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CounterEvent
---@field name? string Required. The name of the counter event.
---@field reportingName? string Required. The name used to identify this counter event in reports.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CounterEventList gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CounterEvent[]

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreateAdvertisersCampaignsRequest
---@field campaignFlight? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CampaignFlight Required. The planned spend and duration of the campaign.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the campaign. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field campaignBudgets? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CampaignBudgetList The list of budgets available to this campaign. If this field is not set, the campaign uses an unlimited budget.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the campaign.
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CampaignEntityStatusEnum|string Required. Controls whether or not the insertion orders under this campaign can spend their budgets and bid on inventory. * Accepted values are `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE`, `ENTITY_STATUS_ARCHIVED`, and `ENTITY_STATUS_PAUSED`. * For CreateCampaign method, `ENTITY_STATUS_ARCHIVED` is not allowed.
---@field campaignGoal? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CampaignGoal Required. The goal of the campaign.
---@field frequencyCap? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.FrequencyCap Required. The frequency cap setting of the campaign. *Warning*: On **February 28, 2025**, frequency cap time periods greater than 30 days will no longer be accepted. [Read more about this announced change](/display-video/api/deprecations#features.lifetime_frequency_cap)
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the campaign was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field campaignId? string Output only. The unique ID of the campaign. Assigned by the system.
---@field advertiserId string Output only. The unique ID of the advertiser the campaign belongs to.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreateAdvertisersChannelsRequest
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the channel.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the channel. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum length of 240 bytes.
---@field channelId? string Output only. The unique ID of the channel. Assigned by the system.
---@field negativelyTargetedLineItemCount? string Output only. Number of line items that are directly targeting this channel negatively.
---@field positivelyTargetedLineItemCount? string Output only. Number of line items that are directly targeting this channel positively.
---@field advertiserId string The ID of the advertiser that owns the created channel.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that owns the created channel.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreateAdvertisersChannelsSitesRequest
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the site.
---@field urlOrAppId? string Required. The app ID or URL of the site. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum length of 240 bytes.
---@field channelId string Required. The ID of the parent channel in which the site will be created.
---@field advertiserId string The ID of the advertiser that owns the parent channel.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that owns the parent channel.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreateAdvertisersCreativesRequest
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the creative. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the creative was last updated, either by the user or system (e.g. creative review). Assigned by the system.
---@field hostingSource? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreativeHostingSourceEnum|string Required. Indicates where the creative is hosted.
---@field html5Video? boolean Output only. Indicates the third-party VAST tag creative requires HTML5 Video support. Output only and only valid for third-party VAST tag creatives. Third-party VAST tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field vpaid? boolean Output only. Indicates the third-party VAST tag creative requires VPAID (Digital Video Player-Ad Interface). Output only and only valid for third-party VAST tag creatives. Third-party VAST tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field creativeType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreativeCreativeTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. The type of the creative.
---@field creativeId? string Output only. The unique ID of the creative. Assigned by the system.
---@field transcodes? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.TranscodeList Output only. Audio/Video transcodes. Display & Video 360 transcodes the main asset into a number of alternative versions that use different file formats or have different properties (resolution, audio bit rate, and video bit rate), each designed for specific video players or bandwidths. These transcodes give a publisher's system more options to choose from for each impression on your video and ensures that the appropriate file serves based on the viewer’s connection and screen size. This field is only supported in the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_VIDEO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO`
---@field expandOnHover? boolean Optional. Indicates the creative will automatically expand on hover. Optional and only valid for third-party expandable creatives. Third-party expandable creatives are creatives with following hosting source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE`
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreativeEntityStatusEnum|string Required. Controls whether or not the creative can serve. Accepted values are: * `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` * `ENTITY_STATUS_ARCHIVED` * `ENTITY_STATUS_PAUSED`
---@field requirePingForAttribution? boolean Optional. Indicates that the creative will wait for a return ping for attribution. Only valid when using a Campaign Manager 360 tracking ad with a third-party ad server parameter and the ${DC_DBM_TOKEN} macro. Optional and only valid for third-party tag creatives or third-party VAST tag creatives. Third-party tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_STANDARD` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE` Third-party VAST tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field skippable? boolean Optional. Whether the user can choose to skip a video creative. This field is only supported for the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field thirdPartyTag? string Optional. The original third-party tag used for the creative. Required and only valid for third-party tag creatives. Third-party tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_STANDARD` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE`
---@field cmPlacementId? string Output only. The unique ID of the Campaign Manager 360 placement associated with the creative. This field is only applicable for creatives that are synced from Campaign Manager.
---@field cmTrackingAd? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CmTrackingAd Optional. The Campaign Manager 360 tracking ad associated with the creative. Optional for the following creative_type when created by an advertiser that uses both Campaign Manager 360 and third-party ad serving: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_SITE_SQUARE` Output only for other cases.
---@field createTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the creative was created. Assigned by the system.
---@field dimensions? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Dimensions Required. Primary dimensions of the creative. Applicable to all creative types. The value of width_pixels and height_pixels defaults to `0` when creative_type is one of: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_VIDEO`
---@field appendedTag? string Optional. Third-party HTML tracking tag to be appended to the creative tag.
---@field iasCampaignMonitoring? boolean Optional. Indicates whether Integral Ad Science (IAS) campaign monitoring is enabled. To enable this for the creative, make sure the Advertiser.creative_config.ias_client_id has been set to your IAS client ID.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the creative.
---@field mp3Audio? boolean Output only. Indicates the third-party audio creative supports MP3. Output only and only valid for third-party audio creatives. Third-party audio creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO`
---@field integrationCode? string Optional. ID information used to link this creative to an external system. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a length of no more than 10,000 characters.
---@field reviewStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ReviewStatusInfo Output only. The current status of the creative review process.
---@field skipOffset? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.AudioVideoOffset Optional. Amount of time to play the video before the skip button appears. This field is required when skippable is true. This field is only supported for the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field creativeAttributes? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreativeCreativeAttributesItemEnumList Output only. A list of attributes of the creative that is generated by the system.
---@field trackerUrls? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList Optional. Tracking URLs for analytics providers or third-party ad technology vendors. The URLs must start with `https:` (except on inventory that doesn't require SSL compliance). If using macros in your URL, use only macros supported by Display & Video 360. Standard URLs only, no IMG or SCRIPT tags. This field is only writeable in the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_SITE_SQUARE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_VIDEO`
---@field universalAdId? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.UniversalAdId Optional. An optional creative identifier provided by a registry that is unique across all platforms. Universal Ad ID is part of the VAST 4.0 standard. It can be modified after the creative is created. This field is only supported for the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field progressOffset? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.AudioVideoOffset Optional. Amount of time to play the video before counting a view. This field is required when skippable is true. This field is only supported for the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field requireMraid? boolean Optional. Indicates that the creative requires MRAID (Mobile Rich Media Ad Interface Definitions system). Set this if the creative relies on mobile gestures for interactivity, such as swiping or tapping. Optional and only valid for third-party tag creatives. Third-party tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_STANDARD` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE`
---@field requireHtml5? boolean Optional. Indicates that the creative relies on HTML5 to render properly. Optional and only valid for third-party tag creatives. Third-party tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_STANDARD` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE`
---@field thirdPartyUrls? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ThirdPartyUrlList Optional. Tracking URLs from third parties to track interactions with a video creative. This field is only supported for the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_VIDEO`
---@field timerEvents? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.TimerEventList Optional. Timer custom events for a rich media creative. Timers track the time during which a user views and interacts with a specified part of a rich media creative. A creative can have multiple timer events, each timed independently. Leave it empty or unset for creatives containing image assets only.
---@field additionalDimensions? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.DimensionsList Optional. Additional dimensions. Applicable when creative_type is one of: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_STANDARD` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_SITE_SQUARE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_LIGHTBOX` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_PUBLISHER_HOSTED` If this field is specified, width_pixels and height_pixels are both required and must be greater than or equal to 0.
---@field notes? string Optional. User notes for this creative. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a length of no more than 20,000 characters.
---@field syntheticContentAttestationStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreativeSyntheticContentAttestationStatusEnum|string Optional. Whether to add a label to the creative as created or edited using AI when served in regions with local AI labeling regulations.
---@field lineItemIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList Output only. The IDs of the line items this creative is associated with. To associate a creative to a line item, use LineItem.creative_ids instead.
---@field counterEvents? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CounterEventList Optional. Counter events for a rich media creative. Counters track the number of times that a user interacts with any part of a rich media creative in a specified way (mouse-overs, mouse-outs, clicks, taps, data loading, keyboard entries, etc.). Any event that can be captured in the creative can be recorded as a counter. Leave it empty or unset for creatives containing image assets only.
---@field dynamic? boolean Output only. Indicates whether the creative is dynamic.
---@field companionCreativeIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList Optional. The IDs of companion creatives for a video creative. You can assign existing display creatives (with image or HTML5 assets) to serve surrounding the publisher's video player. Companions display around the video player while the video is playing and remain after the video has completed. Creatives contain additional dimensions can not be companion creatives. This field is only supported for the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field expandingDirection? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreativeExpandingDirectionEnum|string Optional. Specifies the expanding direction of the creative. Required and only valid for third-party expandable creatives. Third-party expandable creatives are creatives with following hosting source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_EXPANDABLE`
---@field jsTrackerUrl? string Optional. JavaScript measurement URL from supported third-party verification providers (ComScore, DoubleVerify, IAS, Moat). HTML script tags are not supported. This field is only writeable in the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_SITE_SQUARE` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_VIDEO`
---@field mediaDuration? string Output only. Media duration of the creative. Applicable when creative_type is one of: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_NATIVE_VIDEO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_PUBLISHER_HOSTED`
---@field exitEvents? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ExitEventList Required. Exit events for this creative. An exit (also known as a click tag) is any area in your creative that someone can click or tap to open an advertiser's landing page. Every creative must include at least one exit. You can add an exit to your creative in any of the following ways: * Use Google Web Designer's tap area. * Define a JavaScript variable called "clickTag". * Use the Enabler (Enabler.exit()) to track exits in rich media formats.
---@field assets? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.AssetAssociationList Required. Assets associated to this creative.
---@field oggAudio? boolean Output only. Indicates the third-party audio creative supports OGG. Output only and only valid for third-party audio creatives. Third-party audio creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO`
---@field obaIcon? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ObaIcon Optional. Specifies the OBA icon for a video creative. This field is only supported in the following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field vastTagUrl? string Optional. The URL of the VAST tag for a third-party VAST tag creative. Required and only valid for third-party VAST tag creatives. Third-party VAST tag creatives are creatives with following hosting_source: * `HOSTING_SOURCE_THIRD_PARTY` combined with following creative_type: * `CREATIVE_TYPE_AUDIO` * `CREATIVE_TYPE_VIDEO`
---@field advertiserId string Output only. The unique ID of the advertiser the creative belongs to.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreateAdvertisersInsertionOrdersRequest
---@field budget? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudget Required. The budget allocation settings of the insertion order.
---@field bidStrategy? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.BiddingStrategy Optional. The bidding strategy of the insertion order. By default, fixed_bid is set. If the budget field automationType is set to `INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_BUDGET` or `INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_BID_BUDGET`, the insertion order will impose this bidding strategy on its line items. If an imposed bidding strategy is not compatible with a line item's enableOptimizedTargeting setting, the optimized targeting setting will be updated.
---@field performanceGoal? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PerformanceGoal Required. Performance goal of the insertion order.
---@field partnerCosts? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PartnerCostList Optional. The partner costs associated with the insertion order. If absent or empty in CreateInsertionOrder method, the newly created insertion order will inherit partner costs from the partner settings.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the insertion order was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the insertion order.
---@field insertionOrderType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderInsertionOrderTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of insertion order. If this field is unspecified in creation, the value defaults to `RTB`.
---@field integrationDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.IntegrationDetails Optional. Additional integration details of the insertion order.
---@field campaignId? string Required. Immutable. The unique ID of the campaign that the insertion order belongs to.
---@field frequencyCap? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.FrequencyCap Required. The frequency capping setting of the insertion order.
---@field reservationType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderReservationTypeEnum|string Output only. The reservation type of the insertion order.
---@field insertionOrderId? string Output only. The unique ID of the insertion order. Assigned by the system.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the insertion order. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field billableOutcome? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBillableOutcomeEnum|string Immutable. The billable outcome of the insertion order. Outcome based buying is deprecated. `BILLABLE_OUTCOME_PAY_PER_IMPRESSION` is the only valid value.
---@field pacing? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Pacing Required. The budget spending speed setting of the insertion order. pacing_type `PACING_TYPE_ASAP` is not compatible with pacing_period `PACING_PERIOD_FLIGHT`.
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderEntityStatusEnum|string Required. Controls whether or not the insertion order can spend its budget and bid on inventory. * For CreateInsertionOrder method, only `ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT` is allowed. To activate an insertion order, use UpdateInsertionOrder method and update the status to `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` after creation. * An insertion order cannot be changed back to `ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT` status from any other status. * An insertion order cannot be set to `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` if its parent campaign is not active.
---@field advertiserId string Output only. The unique ID of the advertiser the insertion order belongs to.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CreateAdvertisersLineItemsRequest
---@field conversionCounting? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ConversionCountingConfig The conversion tracking setting of the line item.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the line item. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field flight? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemFlight Required. The start and end time of the line item's flight.
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemEntityStatusEnum|string Required. Controls whether or not the line item can spend its budget and bid on inventory. * For CreateLineItem method, only `ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT` is allowed. To activate a line item, use UpdateLineItem method and update the status to `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` after creation. * A line item cannot be changed back to `ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT` status from any other status. * If the line item's parent insertion order is not active, the line item can't spend its budget even if its own status is `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE`.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the line item was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field reservationType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemReservationTypeEnum|string Output only. The reservation type of the line item.
---@field mobileApp? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.MobileApp The mobile app promoted by the line item. This is applicable only when line_item_type is either `LINE_ITEM_TYPE_DISPLAY_MOBILE_APP_INSTALL` or `LINE_ITEM_TYPE_VIDEO_MOBILE_APP_INSTALL`.
---@field frequencyCap? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.FrequencyCap Optional. Required if the line item type is not `LINE_ITEM_TYPE_DEMAND_GEN`. The impression frequency cap settings of the line item. The max_impressions field in this settings object must be used if assigning a limited cap.
---@field bidStrategy? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.BiddingStrategy Required. The bidding strategy of the line item.
---@field warningMessages? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemWarningMessagesItemEnumList Output only. The warning messages generated by the line item. These warnings do not block saving the line item, but some may block the line item from running.
---@field partnerCosts? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PartnerCostList The partner costs associated with the line item. If absent or empty in CreateLineItem method, the newly created line item will inherit partner costs from its parent insertion order.
---@field lineItemId? string Output only. The unique ID of the line item. Assigned by the system.
---@field demandGenSettings? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.DemandGenSettings Optional. Settings specific to Demand Gen line items. Only applicable to Demand Gen line items.
---@field partnerRevenueModel? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PartnerRevenueModel Required. The partner revenue model setting of the line item.
---@field integrationDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.IntegrationDetails Integration details of the line item.
---@field lineItemType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemLineItemTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. The type of the line item.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the line item.
---@field excludeNewExchanges? boolean Whether to exclude new exchanges from automatically being targeted by the line item. This field is false by default.
---@field budget? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemBudget Required. The budget allocation setting of the line item.
---@field youtubeAndPartnersSettings? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.YoutubeAndPartnersSettings Optional. Settings specific to YouTube and Partners line items.
---@field creativeIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList The IDs of the creatives associated with the line item.
---@field pacing? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Pacing Required. The budget spending speed setting of the line item.
---@field insertionOrderId? string Required. Immutable. The unique ID of the insertion order that the line item belongs to.
---@field campaignId? string Output only. The unique ID of the campaign that the line item belongs to.
---@field optimizeFixedBidding? boolean Optional. Whether to enable DV360's bid optimization for fixed bid line items. By default, DV360 optimizes your fixed bid by automatically lowering bids for impressions that are less likely to perform well. This optimization is enabled by default (value is true). When this field is set to `false`, this optimization is disabled, and the bid will not be lowered for any reason. This setting only applies to line items with a `bidding_strategy` of type `FIXED_BID`.
---@field containsEuPoliticalAds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LineItemContainsEuPoliticalAdsEnum|string Whether this line item will serve European Union political ads. If contains_eu_political_ads has been set to `DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING` in the parent advertiser, then this field will be assigned `DOES_NOT_CONTAIN_EU_POLITICAL_ADVERTISING` if not otherwise specified. This field can then be updated using the UI, API, or Structured Data Files. This field must be assigned when creating a new line item. Otherwise, **the `advertisers.lineItems.create` request will fail**.
---@field targetingExpansion? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.TargetingExpansionConfig The [optimized targeting](//support.google.com/displayvideo/answer/12060859) settings of the line item. This config is only applicable for display, video, or audio line items that use automated bidding and positively target eligible audience lists.
---@field advertiserId string Output only. The unique ID of the advertiser the line item belongs to.

