---A single insertion order.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrder
---@field budget? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudget Required. The budget allocation settings of the insertion order.
---@field bidStrategy? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.BiddingStrategy Optional. The bidding strategy of the insertion order. By default, fixed_bid is set. If the budget field automationType is set to `INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_BUDGET` or `INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_BID_BUDGET`, the insertion order will impose this bidding strategy on its line items. If an imposed bidding strategy is not compatible with a line item's enableOptimizedTargeting setting, the optimized targeting setting will be updated.
---@field advertiserId? string Output only. The unique ID of the advertiser the insertion order belongs to.
---@field performanceGoal? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PerformanceGoal Required. Performance goal of the insertion order.
---@field partnerCosts? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PartnerCostList Optional. The partner costs associated with the insertion order. If absent or empty in CreateInsertionOrder method, the newly created insertion order will inherit partner costs from the partner settings.
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the insertion order was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the insertion order.
---@field insertionOrderType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderInsertionOrderTypeEnum Optional. The type of insertion order. If this field is unspecified in creation, the value defaults to `RTB`.
---@field integrationDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.IntegrationDetails Optional. Additional integration details of the insertion order.
---@field campaignId? string Required. Immutable. The unique ID of the campaign that the insertion order belongs to.
---@field frequencyCap? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.FrequencyCap Required. The frequency capping setting of the insertion order.
---@field reservationType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderReservationTypeEnum Output only. The reservation type of the insertion order.
---@field insertionOrderId? string Output only. The unique ID of the insertion order. Assigned by the system.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the insertion order. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field billableOutcome? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBillableOutcomeEnum Immutable. The billable outcome of the insertion order. Outcome based buying is deprecated. `BILLABLE_OUTCOME_PAY_PER_IMPRESSION` is the only valid value.
---@field pacing? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Pacing Required. The budget spending speed setting of the insertion order. pacing_type `PACING_TYPE_ASAP` is not compatible with pacing_period `PACING_PERIOD_FLIGHT`.
---@field entityStatus? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderEntityStatusEnum Required. Controls whether or not the insertion order can spend its budget and bid on inventory. * For CreateInsertionOrder method, only `ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT` is allowed. To activate an insertion order, use UpdateInsertionOrder method and update the status to `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` after creation. * An insertion order cannot be changed back to `ENTITY_STATUS_DRAFT` status from any other status. * An insertion order cannot be set to `ENTITY_STATUS_ACTIVE` if its parent campaign is not active.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBillableOutcomeEnum "BILLABLE_OUTCOME_UNSPECIFIED"|"BILLABLE_OUTCOME_PAY_PER_IMPRESSION"|"BILLABLE_OUTCOME_PAY_PER_CLICK"|"BILLABLE_OUTCOME_PAY_PER_VIEWABLE_IMPRESSION"

---Settings that control how insertion order budget is allocated.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudget
---@field budgetSegments? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetSegmentList Required. The list of budget segments. Use a budget segment to specify a specific budget for a given period of time an insertion order is running.
---@field budgetUnit? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetBudgetUnitEnum|string Required. Immutable. The budget unit specifies whether the budget is currency based or impression based.
---@field automationType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetAutomationTypeEnum|string Optional. The type of automation used to manage bid and budget for the insertion order. If this field is unspecified in creation, the value defaults to `INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_NONE`.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetAutomationTypeEnum "INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_BUDGET"|"INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_NONE"|"INSERTION_ORDER_AUTOMATION_TYPE_BID_BUDGET"

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetBudgetUnitEnum "BUDGET_UNIT_UNSPECIFIED"|"BUDGET_UNIT_CURRENCY"|"BUDGET_UNIT_IMPRESSIONS"

---Settings that control the budget of a single budget segment.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetSegment
---@field budgetAmountMicros? string Required. The budget amount the insertion order will spend for the given date_range. The amount is in micros. Must be greater than 0. For example, 500000000 represents 500 standard units of the currency.
---@field description? string Optional. The budget segment description. It can be used to enter Purchase Order information for each budget segment and have that information printed on the invoices. Must be UTF-8 encoded.
---@field campaignBudgetId? string Optional. The budget_id of the campaign budget that this insertion order budget segment is a part of.
---@field dateRange? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.DateRange Required. The start and end date settings of the budget segment. They are resolved relative to the parent advertiser's time zone. * When creating a new budget segment, both `start_date` and `end_date` must be in the future. * An existing budget segment with a `start_date` in the past has a mutable `end_date` but an immutable `start_date`. * `end_date` must be the `start_date` or later, both before the year 2037.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetSegmentList gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InsertionOrderBudgetSegment[]

