---A single invoice.
---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Invoice
---@field budgetSummaries? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.BudgetSummaryList The list of summarized information for each budget associated with this invoice. This field will only be set if the invoice detail level of the corresponding billing profile was set to "Budget level PO".
---@field nonBudgetMicros? string The total amount of costs or adjustments not tied to a particular budget, in micros of the invoice's currency. For example, if currency_code is `USD`, then 1000000 represents one US dollar.
---@field subtotalAmountMicros? string The pre-tax subtotal amount, in micros of the invoice's currency. For example, if currency_code is `USD`, then 1000000 represents one US dollar.
---@field replacedInvoiceIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList The ID(s) of any originally issued invoice that is being cancelled by this invoice, if applicable. Multiple invoices may be listed if those invoices are being consolidated into a single invoice. May appear on invoice PDF as `Replaced invoice numbers`. If corrected_invoice_id is set, this field will be empty.
---@field currencyCode? string The currency used in the invoice in ISO 4217 format.
---@field dueDate? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Displayvideo_Date The date when the invoice is due.
---@field issueDate? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.Displayvideo_Date The date when the invoice was issued.
---@field displayName? string The display name of the invoice.
---@field paymentsAccountId? string The ID of the payments account the invoice belongs to. Appears on the invoice PDF as `Billing Account Number`.
---@field totalTaxAmountMicros? string The sum of all taxes in invoice, in micros of the invoice's currency. For example, if currency_code is `USD`, then 1000000 represents one US dollar.
---@field name? string The resource name of the invoice.
---@field paymentsProfileId? string The ID of the payments profile the invoice belongs to. Appears on the invoice PDF as `Billing ID`.
---@field serviceDateRange? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.DateRange The service start and end dates which are covered by this invoice.
---@field budgetInvoiceGroupingId? string The budget grouping ID for this invoice. This field will only be set if the invoice level of the corresponding billing profile was set to "Budget invoice grouping ID".
---@field invoiceId? string The unique ID of the invoice.
---@field pdfUrl? string The URL to download a PDF copy of the invoice. This URL is user specific and requires a valid OAuth 2.0 access token to access. The access token must be provided in an `Authorization: Bearer` HTTP header and be authorized for one of the following scopes: * `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/display-video-mediaplanning` * `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/display-video` The URL will be valid for 7 days after retrieval of this invoice object or until this invoice is retrieved again.
---@field purchaseOrderNumber? string Purchase order number associated with the invoice.
---@field correctedInvoiceId? string The ID of the original invoice being adjusted by this invoice, if applicable. May appear on the invoice PDF as `Reference invoice number`. If replaced_invoice_ids is set, this field will be empty.
---@field invoiceType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InvoiceInvoiceTypeEnum The type of invoice document.
---@field totalAmountMicros? string The invoice total amount, in micros of the invoice's currency. For example, if currency_code is `USD`, then 1000000 represents one US dollar.

---@alias gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.InvoiceInvoiceTypeEnum "INVOICE_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"INVOICE_TYPE_CREDIT"|"INVOICE_TYPE_INVOICE"

