---@field modelDetails? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CustomBiddingModelDetailsList Output only. The details of custom bidding models for each advertiser who has access. This field may only include the details of the queried advertiser if the algorithm [`owner`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms#CustomBiddingAlgorithm.FIELDS.oneof_owner) is a partner and is being retrieved using an advertiser [`accessor`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms/list#body.QUERY_PARAMETERS.oneof_accessor).
---@field partnerId? string Immutable. The unique ID of the partner that owns the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field advertiserId? string Immutable. The unique ID of the advertiser that owns the custom bidding algorithm.
---@field sharedAdvertiserIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList The IDs of the advertisers who have access to this algorithm. If advertiser_id is set, this field will only consist of that value. This field will not be set if the algorithm [`owner`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms#CustomBiddingAlgorithm.FIELDS.oneof_owner) is a partner and is being retrieved using an advertiser [`accessor`](/display-video/api/reference/rest/v1/customBiddingAlgorithms/list#body.QUERY_PARAMETERS.oneof_accessor).
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.CustomBiddingAlgorithmCustomBiddingAlgorithmTypeEnum|string Required. Immutable. The type of custom bidding algorithm.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the custom bidding algorithm. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The mask to control which fields to update.
---@field customBiddingAlgorithmId string Output only. The unique ID of the custom bidding algorithm. Assigned by the system.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PatchFloodlightGroupsRequest
---@field lookbackWindow? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.LookbackWindow Required. The lookback window for the Floodlight group. Both click_days and impression_days are required. Acceptable values for both are `0` to `90`, inclusive.
---@field customVariables? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.DocumentMap User-defined custom variables owned by the Floodlight group. Use custom Floodlight variables to create reporting data that is tailored to your unique business needs. Custom Floodlight variables use the keys `U1=`, `U2=`, and so on, and can take any values that you choose to pass to them. You can use them to track virtually any type of data that you collect about your customers, such as the genre of movie that a customer purchases, the country to which the item is shipped, and so on. Custom Floodlight variables may not be used to pass any data that could be used or recognized as personally identifiable information (PII). Example: `custom_variables { fields { "U1": value { number_value: 123.4 }, "U2": value { string_value: "MyVariable2" }, "U3": value { string_value: "MyVariable3" } } }` Acceptable values for keys are "U1" through "U100", inclusive. String values must be less than 64 characters long, and cannot contain the following characters: `"<>`.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the Floodlight group.
---@field activeViewConfig? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.ActiveViewVideoViewabilityMetricConfig The Active View video viewability metric configuration for the Floodlight group.
---@field webTagType? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.FloodlightGroupWebTagTypeEnum|string Required. The web tag type enabled for the Floodlight group.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the Floodlight group.
---@field floodlightGroupId string Output only. The unique ID of the Floodlight group. Assigned by the system.
---@field partnerId? string Required. The partner context by which the Floodlight group is being accessed.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The mask to control which fields to update.

---@class gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.PatchGuaranteedOrdersRequest
---@field updateTime? string Output only. The timestamp when the guaranteed order was last updated. Assigned by the system.
---@field defaultAdvertiserId? string Output only. The ID of default advertiser of the guaranteed order. The default advertiser is either the read_write_advertiser_id or, if that is not set, the first advertiser listed in read_advertiser_ids. Otherwise, there is no default advertiser.
---@field name? string Output only. The resource name of the guaranteed order.
---@field displayName? string Required. The display name of the guaranteed order. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field readAdvertiserIds? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.StringList The IDs of advertisers with read access to the guaranteed order. This field must not include the advertiser assigned to read_write_advertiser_id if it is set. All advertisers in this field must belong to read_write_partner_id or the same partner as read_write_advertiser_id.
---@field defaultCampaignId? string The ID of the default campaign that is assigned to the guaranteed order. The default campaign must belong to the default advertiser.
---@field legacyGuaranteedOrderId? string Output only. The legacy ID of the guaranteed order. Assigned by the original exchange. The legacy ID is unique within one exchange, but is not guaranteed to be unique across all guaranteed orders. This ID is used in SDF and UI.
---@field readWriteAdvertiserId? string The advertiser with read/write access to the guaranteed order. This is also the default advertiser of the guaranteed order.
---@field publisherName? string Required. The publisher name of the guaranteed order. Must be UTF-8 encoded with a maximum size of 240 bytes.
---@field status? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.GuaranteedOrderStatus The status settings of the guaranteed order.
---@field readAccessInherited? boolean Whether all advertisers of read_write_partner_id have read access to the guaranteed order. Only applicable if read_write_partner_id is set. If True, overrides read_advertiser_ids.
---@field exchange? gcp.unstable.displayvideo_v2.GuaranteedOrderExchangeEnum|string Required. Immutable. The exchange where the guaranteed order originated.
---@field readWritePartnerId? string The partner with read/write access to the guaranteed order.
---@field partnerId? string The ID of the partner that the request is being made within.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The mask to control which fields to update.
---@field advertiserId? string The ID of the advertiser that the request is being made within.
---@field guaranteedOrderId string Output only. The unique identifier of the guaranteed order. The guaranteed order IDs have the format `{exchange}-{legacy_guaranteed_order_id}`.

